From c1be176c47c6d9caef5e0d91b410bbdc1846c764 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:15:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: provider allowlist and OpenRouter failover

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: expose and enforce provider-family execution allowlist
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: upstream-candidate
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 0004-candidate-provider-allowlist-and-openrouter-failover.patch

Patch intent:
Add a provider-family execution allowlist that gates model switching,
persisted routes, dispatch, failover, and all direct memory-sidecar egress.
Empty or absent means unrestricted; a non-empty list fails closed for unknown
identities. Picker-visibility methods also respect the allowlist so routes
for denied families are hidden, but this is a side effect of execution policy,
not a separate visibility filter.

Why it exists:
Keeps sessions inside explicit provider allowlists, including auxiliary
sidecar calls that would otherwise bypass main-provider dispatch. Non-goal is
restricting picker visibility only; the picker narrowing is a separate config
field that cannot grant execution the allowlist denies.

Tests that register the process-global active provider could leak that
registration into later tests in the same process. A cfg(test)
ActiveProviderTestGuard RAII captures and clears the exact stored
registration and restores it on drop, including during unwinds, so guarded
tests get a deterministic provider state and clean up even when they fail.
The caller must already hold the test-state lock
(crate::storage::lock_test_env()), which serializes access to the global.
The guard is test-only support; production provider behavior is unchanged.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs adds the allowed_providers field.
crates/jcode-provider-core/src/lib.rs defines ProviderFamily,
ProviderFamilyPolicy,
provider_family() methods on RuntimeKey and ModelRouteApiMethod.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/mod.rs enforces policy in set_model and route
filtering, and in available_providers_for_model and provider_details_for_model.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/dispatch.rs and multi_provider.rs enforce policy
at dispatch and failover boundaries.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/catalog_memo.rs projects cached routes under
policy;
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/catalog_remote_routes.rs and catalog_routes.rs
filter names-only remote and full catalog routes by runtime family.
crates/jcode-base/src/sidecar.rs applies policy to automatic selection, explicit
sidecar constructors, and direct-backend fallbacks.
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/policy_tests.rs and sidecar.rs cover policy
enforcement, including denied jcode auth/import through dispatch, failover,
sidecar, and model switching. crates/jcode-base/src/provider/jcode.rs also
blocks direct jcode model switching when its family is denied.
crates/jcode-protocol/src/wire/events.rs carries runtime identity through
names-only catalog events. crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs
documents
the policy.

Test isolation uses the cfg(test) ActiveProviderTestGuard in
crates/jcode-base/src/provider/mod.rs; policy_tests.rs and sidecar.rs tests
use it instead of leaving a registered provider behind, and
sidecar_provider_backend_delegates_to_main_dispatch_for_policy clears it to
get a deterministic no-provider window.

Update guidance:
Keep ProviderFamily taxonomy exhaustive. OpenRouterEu is a forward-compatible
variant that the OpenRouter EU patch maps a runtime to. Apply this policy to
all direct provider clients, not just main dispatch. The policy must fail
closed for unknown entries and preserve empty-list legacy behavior. Keep
ActiveProviderTestGuard cfg(test)-only: it must restore the exact previous
registration on drop, including during unwinds, and require the caller to
hold crate::storage::lock_test_env(). Never add a production clear API.

